A||||1||G25C||Of Lawers and Fieros
Z||000000||G25C||07-28-99||10:25 AM||||<br>Yesterday i was in the Wyandot Court of Common Pleas (the same court used in Stephen Kings movie "THE SHAWSHANK REDEMPTION").  I was there because i filed for custody of my 2 year old daughter.<p>When we broke for lunch, my buddy (who was a witness) asked if he could ride with me.  Of course i said yes, I enjoy giving people rides in my 87 GT.  My buddy Jason was at my car when i came out of the court house and i noticed there was a "for sale" sign on the windshield.  Then i noticed that this wasnt my GT but one that looked identical to mine. (same color and interior, the only difference was that this was a 85 GT and was a notch back).<p>As i turned to my lawer and said "look, my buddy at the wrong car" my lawer looked at my Fiero and said thats my car he's standing at.  <p>He has it for sale for 3000, but it sounds like it has an exhaust leak and it as the normal black faded paint. <p>I paid 3100 for my GT and it had 94000 miles on it and was in almost great condition.  Is his price for a 85 GT worth that?  He said he would take best offer also.  I was thinking mabey 2500.<p>what do you think?
Z||000001||87GT||07-28-99||07:41 PM||||I think you got a hell of a deal for $3100 on your 87GT, as far as $3,000 for the 85GT, I have never seen one go that high.  The highest 85GT I have seen was priced at about $2200.  Its up to you. :-)
